00:01:21.940 --> 00:01:24.780
The suspenseful, heart-pounding dance dance
Hara-hara doki-doki dansu dansu

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:28.240
An exhilarating, thrilling chance chance
Uki-uki waku-waku chansu chansu

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:45.100
Ugh, it stinks.

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:48.660
This is all from a single
sewer tank malfunction, too.

00:01:48.770 --> 00:01:49.930
Unbelievable!

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:54.340
Yeah, it's because this is where all the
sewage ends up from the entire tower.

00:01:54.610 --> 00:01:56.280
We have all the space in the universe,

00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:58.910
so why are we living on top of each other?

00:01:59.210 --> 00:02:00.240
Beats me.

00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:02.420
It's because this satellite planet is part of the...

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:04.050
...Federation's environmental
control program, right?

00:02:04.050 --> 00:02:04.850
I see it.

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:22.840
What's this?

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:25.070
How is this a malfunction?

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:59.870
What's This!
My Supple Skin Is a Mess

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:04.250
Two crew members have gone missing
near sewage treatment tank number 4...

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:06.310
...on the B17 sewage system area.

00:03:06.310 --> 00:03:09.910
Security officers in charge of this area
should begin their search immediately.

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:17.190
The other guy looks pretty much the same.

00:03:17.190 --> 00:03:18.260
Do you want to see?

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:19.590
No, thank you.

00:03:19.960 --> 00:03:21.520
Do you have any idea what happened?

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:25.490
This was probably done by some creature.

00:03:25.670 --> 00:03:29.690
However, I have no idea
what kind of creature.

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:31.800
A creature?

00:03:39.410 --> 00:03:40.010
Hello!

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:47.080
We were sent by the 3WA
in response to your request.

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:49.120
As you know, we're the Lovely Angels.

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:52.790
Um, Chief...

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:55.600
Out of all people, they sent you guys again?

00:03:55.600 --> 00:03:56.760
It's over!

00:03:57.130 --> 00:03:58.930
This tower is doomed!

00:03:59.230 --> 00:04:03.190
I'm the most unfortunate
management chief in the galaxy!

00:04:06.110 --> 00:04:06.730
Um...

00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:11.010
You don't know just how terrible these two are!

00:04:11.350 --> 00:04:18.550
They're the ones who completely killed our
main computer and tilted this tower!

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:20.850
Yuri, let's go home.

00:04:21.790 --> 00:04:23.660
That's right! Leave!

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:25.220
Huh?

00:04:25.390 --> 00:04:26.520
Ah, wait, wait, wait...

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:31.060
On second thought, I'm going to hire you.

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:33.560
This job is right up your alley.

00:04:40.010 --> 00:04:41.440
Who does he think he is?

00:04:41.510 --> 00:04:44.310
How is this job "right up our alley"?

00:04:44.610 --> 00:04:48.050
That man has become so crooked. Poor guy.

00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:51.510
Poor us for having to clean a sewer!

00:04:51.950 --> 00:04:52.720
Hey...

00:04:52.950 --> 00:04:53.510
What?

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:56.050
Did you hear something?

00:04:58.130 --> 00:04:58.890
Not really.

00:05:01.060 --> 00:05:01.720
See?

00:05:05.530 --> 00:05:06.370
Should we check it out?

00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:07.440
Of course!

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:07.900
Come on.

00:05:07.900 --> 00:05:08.470
W-What?
Come on.

00:05:08.470 --> 00:05:09.100
W-What?

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:23.880
Kei!

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:25.220
Can't believe I fell...

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:26.740
It's slippery, so be careful.

00:05:27.590 --> 00:05:29.580
Dummy! Don't scare me like that.

00:05:29.720 --> 00:05:31.720
Then why don't you go first?

00:05:35.800 --> 00:05:37.530
H-Help me...

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:41.370
What happened?

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:50.270
Gross!

00:06:08.830 --> 00:06:11.130
I finally got rid of that sewer smell.

00:06:11.130 --> 00:06:12.570
We're going back down there anyway,

00:06:12.570 --> 00:06:15.430
so why even bother scrubbing
yourself squeaky clean?

00:06:15.900 --> 00:06:17.570
This is why you're no good.

00:06:17.570 --> 00:06:18.470
What do you mean?

00:06:18.940 --> 00:06:22.000
Would you want to date a guy
who smells like a sewer?

00:06:24.910 --> 00:06:27.680
Well, at least we'll have each other, right?

00:06:28.350 --> 00:06:29.480
What's that?

00:06:29.720 --> 00:06:32.850
It's a flamethrower, but a
much more compact model.

00:06:33.050 --> 00:06:35.720
You're going to burn an aquatic creature to death?

00:06:35.720 --> 00:06:37.030
Isn't that a bit too simple?

00:06:37.030 --> 00:06:40.800
The flame from this gun won't
go out and it inhibits skin respiration,

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:43.130
so it's much more effective than a heat gun.

00:06:46.070 --> 00:06:46.690
Yes?

00:06:48.070 --> 00:06:48.870
A corpse?

00:06:57.050 --> 00:06:58.600
The drone brought it back.

00:06:58.710 --> 00:06:59.680
The drone did?

00:07:00.550 --> 00:07:03.780
Yes. It was probably already
dead by the time the drone found it.

00:07:04.390 --> 00:07:06.390
Which means, you did your job.

00:07:06.390 --> 00:07:08.880
And without destroying the place, for once!

00:07:09.020 --> 00:07:10.720
This is reason to celebrate.

00:07:11.230 --> 00:07:12.090
We're not done yet.

00:07:12.090 --> 00:07:13.150
What?

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:16.660
This isn't the one we saw.

00:07:17.030 --> 00:07:20.990
B-But, it matches the description from your report!

00:07:21.070 --> 00:07:22.260
Jeez, you're slow.

00:07:22.370 --> 00:07:24.700
It means there's more than one.

00:07:24.910 --> 00:07:26.310
How could you be so sure?

00:07:26.610 --> 00:07:27.970
Because it has a head.

00:07:28.310 --> 00:07:29.170
A head?

00:07:29.340 --> 00:07:32.180
It's only been six hours since I blew its head off.

00:07:32.510 --> 00:07:34.950
Do you think it could regenerate that fast?

00:07:36.320 --> 00:07:40.950
It seems to be a type of mutated mollusk
that's commonly found in the Lovecraft System.

00:07:41.020 --> 00:07:41.850
Keep going.

00:07:43.490 --> 00:07:45.160
Considering what type of creature it is,

00:07:45.160 --> 00:07:47.260
it shouldn't have that kind of regeneration ability.

00:07:47.260 --> 00:07:48.430
See?

00:07:48.430 --> 00:07:51.330
Our job has only begun.

00:07:51.870 --> 00:07:53.600
H-How many are there?

00:07:53.770 --> 00:07:54.860
Who knows.

00:07:55.040 --> 00:07:56.910
Maybe one, maybe a hundred...

00:07:56.910 --> 00:07:59.170
Or maybe a lot more... I guess!

00:08:01.010 --> 00:08:02.340
T-This is a nightmare!

00:08:02.680 --> 00:08:04.110
Don't worry.

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:06.440
We'll wake you up.

00:08:06.610 --> 00:08:07.840
Leave it to us.
Leave it to us.

00:08:09.580 --> 00:08:11.850
The cause of death is thought to be from...

00:08:11.850 --> 00:08:16.380
...the destruction of the cuticular
layer of the skin by a certain acid.

00:08:16.620 --> 00:08:22.260
Another important point is that the creature's
body was found in the B16 cesspool.

00:08:22.730 --> 00:08:27.690
This is where the industrial wastewater
from the tower ends up.

00:08:27.800 --> 00:08:33.540
After running tests on this water,
we've identified the same acid in this cesspool.

00:08:33.540 --> 00:08:35.610
So these idiots, whoever they are,

00:08:35.610 --> 00:08:39.680
routed the industrial wastewater here and
gave us the clue to solving this case?

00:08:39.680 --> 00:08:41.080
E-Exactly!

00:08:41.280 --> 00:08:42.040
Jeez!

00:08:42.820 --> 00:08:44.550
The first phase of our mission...

00:08:44.550 --> 00:08:47.520
...is to drag all the monsters out of the pipes.

00:09:05.270 --> 00:09:05.930
Now!

00:09:25.360 --> 00:09:26.520
Here they come.

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:31.060
Move to phase two.

00:09:31.630 --> 00:09:36.400
These creatures use their cilium to detect
subtle vibrations and to hunt down their prey.

00:09:36.600 --> 00:09:38.240
Using this behavior to our advantage,

00:09:38.240 --> 00:09:40.680
we'll have an underwater speaker
emit a low frequency wave.

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:44.130
By doing so, it'll stimulate their cilia
and we'll be able to lure them into one area.

00:10:09.240 --> 00:10:10.670
There were this many?

00:10:18.280 --> 00:10:20.040
Acid dispersal group, ready.

00:10:20.250 --> 00:10:22.940
Neutralizer dispersal group to B17, ready.

00:10:29.890 --> 00:10:30.980
Disperse the acid!

00:10:54.750 --> 00:10:56.550
Kei, there's something headed your way!

00:10:56.780 --> 00:10:57.380
Huh?

00:10:58.320 --> 00:10:59.510
Hey, Mughi!

00:11:00.860 --> 00:11:01.750
From which way?

00:11:01.990 --> 00:11:03.320
Left. From your left.

00:11:11.470 --> 00:11:12.690
It's closing in!

00:11:13.700 --> 00:11:14.600
Run!

00:11:21.910 --> 00:11:23.570
What the?!

00:11:53.270 --> 00:11:54.470
It shoots acid!

00:11:54.810 --> 00:11:56.870
Save me!

00:11:57.650 --> 00:11:58.480
Damn it!

00:11:59.110 --> 00:12:00.010
Stay back!

00:12:04.890 --> 00:12:05.850
Take this!

00:12:34.380 --> 00:12:36.440
Do you think that killed it?

00:12:37.190 --> 00:12:39.650
I hate to say this, but I doubt it.

00:12:39.720 --> 00:12:40.760
We're in agreement then.

00:12:40.760 --> 00:12:42.050
So, what's next?

00:12:42.620 --> 00:12:46.460
We're going to come up with our next move
over a cup of warm cinnamon tea.

00:12:46.830 --> 00:12:48.820
While you're at it, admit that you failed.

00:12:49.830 --> 00:12:52.700
What's with you? That's such a nasty thing to say!

00:12:53.300 --> 00:12:56.240
Do you know what you've done?

00:12:57.710 --> 00:12:59.610
Chief, everyone is exhausted.

00:12:59.610 --> 00:13:00.980
There's no need to raise your voice.

00:13:00.980 --> 00:13:03.980
In a way, it was a success,
since we got rid of those mollusks.

00:13:03.980 --> 00:13:05.710
That's the problem!

00:13:05.780 --> 00:13:10.740
It's obvious those mollusks were just
food for that other one! Am I right?

00:13:10.950 --> 00:13:13.350
Yes, that's probably the case.

00:13:13.760 --> 00:13:14.690
Good.

00:13:15.020 --> 00:13:18.530
But you! You killed off its food!

00:13:18.530 --> 00:13:20.090
Now think!

00:13:20.090 --> 00:13:22.760
What do you think that creature will do
now that its food source is gone?

00:13:22.760 --> 00:13:25.390
It might come above ground in search of food.

00:13:25.530 --> 00:13:29.900
The ones we were dealing with were about
three meters long, a little bigger than us, but...

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:33.100
Now we have to live in fear of
a thirty-meter-long monster.

00:13:33.170 --> 00:13:35.240
We know what you're trying to say, but...

00:13:35.240 --> 00:13:37.410
...none of us knew that thing was down there...
...none of us knew that thing was down there...

00:13:37.410 --> 00:13:39.040
...until a few moments ago!
...until a few moments ago!

00:13:41.220 --> 00:13:43.550
This is all because you two
didn't adequately investigate it...

00:13:43.550 --> 00:13:45.490
...before you went ahead with your plan!

00:13:45.820 --> 00:13:47.310
After all, you two are the Dirty...

00:13:48.890 --> 00:13:50.390
Oh, my. Sorry about that.

00:13:50.390 --> 00:13:51.260
Yuri, let's go.

00:13:51.260 --> 00:13:51.760
Okay.

00:13:51.760 --> 00:13:54.660
Oww...

00:14:08.940 --> 00:14:12.240
This is exactly what I was afraid of.

00:14:19.490 --> 00:14:20.780
Find anything?

00:14:24.630 --> 00:14:25.250
Hey.

00:14:26.490 --> 00:14:30.260
If it feeds off of mollusks
from the Lovecraft system,

00:14:30.260 --> 00:14:32.600
it must be from the same planetary system.

00:14:32.670 --> 00:14:35.140
Most likely, it's a mutation
of a sea slug species.

00:14:37.210 --> 00:14:39.510
But that's all the data there is on it,

00:14:39.510 --> 00:14:42.370
apart from it having positive phototaxis behaviors.

00:14:42.440 --> 00:14:44.430
In other words, it's attracted to light?

00:14:45.980 --> 00:14:47.310
That's good to know.

00:14:48.050 --> 00:14:50.380
So, what is it doing here?

00:14:50.450 --> 00:14:51.280
Who knows?

00:14:53.390 --> 00:14:57.980
Let's see..."A few were smuggled off
of their native planets as pets."

00:14:59.160 --> 00:15:01.420
How fun could they be as pets?

00:15:01.730 --> 00:15:03.300
They must have escaped
after they were abandoned...

00:15:03.300 --> 00:15:04.730
...or when their owners grew tired of them.

00:15:04.730 --> 00:15:06.430
That's so sad.

00:15:07.540 --> 00:15:11.340
People shouldn't own pets if they're
going to abandon them, right Mughi?

00:15:13.440 --> 00:15:15.710
It's probably hungry.

00:15:17.750 --> 00:15:20.650
We could probably lure it out easily now...

00:15:20.650 --> 00:15:22.620
...if we use some bait, don't you think?

00:15:22.680 --> 00:15:23.480
No way!

00:15:23.750 --> 00:15:26.150
You're not thinking about
using Mughi as bait, are you?

00:15:26.550 --> 00:15:27.490
I am.

00:15:27.620 --> 00:15:28.780
Quit it!

00:15:28.920 --> 00:15:30.590
If you're going to use Mughi as bait...

00:15:30.590 --> 00:15:31.930
You'll do it instead?

00:15:31.930 --> 00:15:32.520
Yeah!

00:15:33.930 --> 00:15:35.560
Okay, it's settled then!

00:15:39.870 --> 00:15:40.730
Rock, paper, scissors!

00:15:40.970 --> 00:15:42.900
I win! You're the bait!

00:15:43.070 --> 00:15:44.300
S-Shoot...

00:15:46.510 --> 00:15:50.170
So, the two of you and that cat will act as bait?

00:15:51.880 --> 00:15:54.110
The three of us will enter
the sewer system by ourselves.

00:15:54.250 --> 00:15:55.910
You won't object to that, right?

00:15:57.290 --> 00:15:58.620
What are the conditions?

00:15:59.820 --> 00:16:01.580
It's all written here.

00:16:03.760 --> 00:16:07.020
Also, we need you to turn off
all the lights in the sewer system.

00:16:07.800 --> 00:16:08.890
Anything else?

00:16:09.630 --> 00:16:11.000
A secure communication line.

00:16:11.700 --> 00:16:13.030
That should do it, right?

00:16:13.130 --> 00:16:14.190
It should.

00:16:15.670 --> 00:16:16.690
Consider it done.

00:16:31.190 --> 00:16:33.790
Watching trash isn't so boring, after all.

00:16:33.790 --> 00:16:35.720
Sure, as long as it doesn't stink.

00:16:36.690 --> 00:16:37.660
Do you think it'll come?

00:16:37.660 --> 00:16:40.960
If it doesn't, we're nothing
but idiots for sitting in the sewer.

00:16:41.060 --> 00:16:45.100
But what if it liked what it ate at
the pool and stayed above ground...

00:16:45.100 --> 00:16:47.440
...instead of coming back down to the sewer?

00:16:47.440 --> 00:16:50.710
You're so sharp! To tell the truth,
I was wondering that too.

00:16:50.710 --> 00:16:52.040
W-What? You're telling me this now?

00:16:52.040 --> 00:16:53.440
Oh, what to do...

00:17:03.850 --> 00:17:05.480
This wasn't part of the plan!

00:17:51.600 --> 00:17:52.830
It's coming after us!

00:17:54.140 --> 00:17:55.630
It's giving me goosebumps.

00:18:15.320 --> 00:18:17.290
They finished connecting the valves.

00:18:17.290 --> 00:18:17.990
Good.

00:18:17.990 --> 00:18:22.900
Close lines E 402 and 403
leading to B16 and B17.

00:18:22.960 --> 00:18:24.300
Release the compressed air.

00:18:24.300 --> 00:18:24.920
Yes, sir.

00:18:31.040 --> 00:18:31.870
It's begun!

00:18:31.870 --> 00:18:32.960
Kei, finish it!

00:18:33.570 --> 00:18:34.560
Leave it to me!

00:18:36.780 --> 00:18:38.300
The Dirty Pair have passed
the designated point.

00:18:39.180 --> 00:18:40.650
Release the liquid nitrogen.

00:18:54.030 --> 00:18:54.960
We did it!

00:19:01.800 --> 00:19:03.240
We did it... right?

00:19:03.240 --> 00:19:04.360
Dunno.

00:19:19.450 --> 00:19:20.420
W-W-W...

00:19:20.720 --> 00:19:21.920
What the?

00:19:39.440 --> 00:19:41.010
It regenerated.

00:19:41.010 --> 00:19:42.010
Continue the mission as planned!

00:19:42.010 --> 00:19:43.980
Our target is still mighty healthy!

00:19:44.310 --> 00:19:46.370
Release the liquid nitrogen from UH3.

00:19:52.090 --> 00:19:53.110
It's so not cute!

00:19:53.450 --> 00:19:55.720
Hey, we want to finish this quickly.

00:19:55.720 --> 00:19:57.020
Can't you do something?

00:19:57.360 --> 00:19:59.160
They're heading towards
the AR rendezvous point.

00:19:59.360 --> 00:20:00.620
It's no use. It's too far.

00:20:01.530 --> 00:20:03.120
Guide them to Pool D.

00:20:03.200 --> 00:20:04.530
But Chief, that's...

00:20:05.070 --> 00:20:06.230
That's our only option!

00:20:06.230 --> 00:20:07.720
Where are we supposed to go?

00:20:08.940 --> 00:20:11.030
The waterway will soon split into
two and you want to go left.

00:20:11.110 --> 00:20:11.900
Go left.

00:20:14.480 --> 00:20:15.970
Release the liquid nitrogen.

00:20:19.350 --> 00:20:20.340
Entry confirmed.

00:20:24.220 --> 00:20:25.010
Release it!

00:20:45.310 --> 00:20:46.010
You ready?

00:20:46.010 --> 00:20:46.500
Yeah!

00:20:47.580 --> 00:20:48.440
Take that!

00:21:33.750 --> 00:21:34.950
